                        "content": "A client has just been told by the primary health care provider about a diagnosis of breast cancer. The client responds, \"Oh, no! Does this mean I'm going to die?\" The nurse interprets the client's initial reaction as which response?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nThe client's reaction is one of fear. The client has verbalized the object of fear (dying), which makes anxiety incorrect. There is no evidence of rage or denial in the client's statement.",
